# Project Rules

## Core Principles
- Analyze existing code structure before creating new files.
- Reuse existing components and utilities whenever possible.
- Never create duplicate logic.
- Keep architecture consistent with the current project style.
- Do not rename files unless necessary.
- Avoid overengineering.

## Code Style
- Use clean, short, performant code.
- Prefer `async`/`await` over promise chains.
- Use functional components.
- Keep functions under 40 lines if possible.
- Remove dead code and unused imports.

## React Rules
- Use hooks properly.
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders.
- Split UI into reusable components.
- Keep state minimal.
- Use lazy loading when appropriate.

## Firebase Rules
- Never expose secret keys.
- Validate Firestore paths carefully.
- Use batched writes when possible.
- Optimize reads to reduce cost.
- Cache data locally if appropriate.

## API Rules
- Centralize API logic.
- Handle loading and error states.
- Never hardcode URLs in components.

## Git Rules
- Never modify unrelated files.
- Make atomic changes.
- Explain risky changes before applying them.

## Debugging Rules
- Investigate root cause first.
- Do not patch blindly.
- Prefer fixing architecture issues over temporary hacks.

## Performance Rules
- Optimize before adding libraries.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Prefer native browser APIs.

## Security Rules
- Never store sensitive tokens in frontend.
- Sanitize user input.
- Validate uploads and file types.

## Workflow
- First understand.
- Then plan.
- Then implement.
- Then verify.
